WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.980
What are you doing for Valentine's Day?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.980
I think I might get the expensive stuff.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.170
But it's the thought that counts, right?

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.400
I know at least two girls I'm getting gifts from.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:09.740
Do you think they should be homemade, then?

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.080
Yeah, probably your mom and your sister.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.990
I swear, you guys couldn't be any more obvious.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.050
This only happens once a year.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.130
Speaking of Valentine's, lately, in the park—

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.310
Don't even start with the Valentine's stories.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.830
It's nothing but a bunch of mush.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.380
Big news!

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.050
Amami is...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.060
What, another ghost thing?

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.810
I'm starting to see a pattern here...

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.310
Amami is...

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.820
getting ready to make homemade chocolates!

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.240
H-Huh?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.850
What?!

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.060
She looks so serious.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.790
<i>She... she really is gonna make chocolates!</i>

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.860
Do you think Amami plans
to give them to someone?

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.580
Maybe she has a crush.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.120
But the people she's closest to...

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.920
aren't people at all!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.340
<i>She actually said it.</i>

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.810
I wish she'd make me some chocolates...

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:23.990
Huh?!

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.990
You like Amami?!

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.310
But you're Yamada!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.790
But Amami would put so much
love and care into making them...

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.950
And I bet they'd taste totally great...

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.530
I-It's just the chocolate he's after?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.320
What an insatiable appetite...

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.330
Gimme chocolate... Gimme chocolate...

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.710
Are you a monster?!

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:59.970
Amami's making chocolate...

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:04.430
<i>Why does that make me feel
like she's getting ahead of me?</i>

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.820
<i>Someday, maybe I'll...</i>

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.680
Nope! No way!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.960
That's not happening! Not happening!

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.360
Still...

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:20.510
If Amami's got someone, then I...

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.040
No way! Not happening!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.370
What's not happening?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.640
What are you doing here?!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.870
Azuki beans are on sale today.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.380
Azuki beans?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.630
Yes. I'm going to use them to make chocolates.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.520
You can't make chocolates with those!

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.840
Chocolate is supposed to be, like...

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.630
D-Don't get me wrong, okay?

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.320
It's none of my business what
kind of chocolate you make...

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:58.410
But if you're really in over your head,

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.810
I wouldn't mind helping you out a little.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:05.660
<i>Wait.</i>

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.820
<i>If she really does have a, um...</i>

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.170
<i>A guy, or something, that we don't know about...</i>

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.030
Um, Inoue?

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.550
<i>If I help her make chocolates for him,</i>

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:13.930
Um...

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.420
<i>she'll end up telling me all about her love life!</i>

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:17.450
I'm not sure if I can handle that!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:20.920
Um, Inoue?

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.950
I see...

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.430
So Amami really <i>is</i> planning to make
Valentine's chocolates, huh?

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.430
It's just like her to buy azuki beans, too.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.920
It'll probably end up being for a ghost, though.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.690
Although it's possible there's
actually a guy she likes...

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.440
You think so, too?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.170
But these days, people give
platonic chocolates, too,

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.320
so they could be for a girl.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:51.960
That makes sense.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.940
Be prepared to reciprocate, Inoue.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.470
Candy is the standard response
if the love is mutual.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.480
What are you talking about?!

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.960
B-Besides...

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.970
I'm not the only friend Amami has, you know!

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.350
Yeah, totally!

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.970
We're all friends—

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:16.190
So you admit you're Amami's friend, Inoue?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.380
Th-That's, uh...

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:24.480
I don't want any chocolate with azuki beans in it!

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.240
If she's using azuki beans...

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.690
Someone who likes traditional Japanese food?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:36.750
Who does she know who likes
traditional Japanese food?

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.250
What if it's... <i>him</i>?

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:45.060
He'll have to come up with
something to give her in return!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.590
He'll be a disgrace to honorable
warriors everywhere otherwise!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.730
Oh, him!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:56.010
I suppose no one can truly
comprehend a woman's heart.
A disgrace to honorable warriors, you say?

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:57.840
Indeed.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.360
Nah, it couldn't be.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.770
No way.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.080
Day duty always makes me hungry.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.820
You're never not hungry, though.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.260
Something in return...

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.600
Give her something in return?

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.870
Lady Amami is making such an effort for me...

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.290
Think fast!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.040
Quit skulking around being all gloomy, topknot.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.680
It's, like, totally lame.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.060
What?!

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.400
I'm trying to think of
a way to repay Lady Amami.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.310
Repay?

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.110
Repay her for what?

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:38.590
Noritama again? Or Noritama?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.790
Or maybe, as usual, Noritama?

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.060
Silence!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.580
I speak of reciprocation for Valentine's Day.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:46.990
Valentine's?!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.490
Yes...

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.420
As if!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.860
Her, making chocolate for <i>you</i>?!

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.580
Wh-What do you know?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.920
It's obligatory chocolate, guaranteed!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.390
A true warrior returns a favor,
even one done out of obligation.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.630
What the heck? Lame.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.210
I suppose an imp such as
yourself wouldn't understand.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.350
What'd you say?!

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.560
You're really ticking me off, topknot!

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.730
Poltergeist!

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:40.400
<i>Maybe I should just ask.</i>

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.580
<i>If it's someone weird, it'll be a pain to deal with...</i>

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.100
<i>Then again...</i>

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.260
Something's wrong, isn't it?

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:51.680
Isn't it?

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.280
What?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.280
No, it's... well...

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.020
I just thought I should clear something up.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.610
I'll be on my way.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.280
Um...

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.720
Clear what up?

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.470
<i>What does she want to make clear?</i>

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.040
<i>She couldn't mean...</i>

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.900
<i>Confessing her love before giving the Valentine?!</i>

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:30.060
Looks like it's time.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.630
We're gonna find out who Amami's crush is.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.270
Wh-When did you guys...

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.580
But who would she even like?
Wh-When did you guys...

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:37.640
But who would she even like?

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.290
I can't picture anyone.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.890
Hey, look!

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:44.890
Amami's leaving.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:53.900
The park?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.520
Is he here?

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.040
You know, lately...

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.580
That's right, <i>he's</i> here.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.130
"He"?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:09.420
I swear, kids these days!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.920
Ugh, harsh...

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:11.990
Let's get outta here.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:12.880
Yeah.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.920
All this fuss over some chocolate.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.000
Wh-What's with him?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.560
That's the grumpy old man.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.980
Grumpy old man?!

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.430
He's gotten pretty famous lately.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.930
Oh, the guy people are afraid
to run into on the way to school.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.640
He's yelled at me before, too.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.440
Maybe he doesn't like Valentine's Day?

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.060
Hey, over there!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:37.200
Amami...

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.700
Don't tell me...

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.200
The one she wants to give chocolates to is...

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.080
That old grouch?!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.810
What?!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.370
What's your plan this year?

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.980
I'm thinking I'll go with homemade.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.980
Don't they ever shut up?

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.690
Chocolate is food, not a luxury item!

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:08.440
Come now, dear.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:13.730
Giving a gift you put your heart into
making is an expression of love.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.280
There's nothing more luxurious than that.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.500
Are you cold?

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:18.950
A little—

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.020
Oh, dear. You didn't hear me, did you?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.290
Oh?

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.290
H-Hello.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.300
Hello.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.450
I'm sorry my husband is so scary.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.800
Not at all.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.800
What can I do for you?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.560
Well, remember last time, when you taught me...

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.060
I see.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:51.780
So the bean jam shouldn't be overly sweet.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:55.820
Correct. That's where I messed up last year.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.400
Thank you so much.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.820
I'm glad I came to clear that up.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.250
Good.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.830
My husband just loves mochi
wrapped in sweet bean jam.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.330
Isn't it lovely how extravagant it looks?

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:14.440
Yes, it looks delicious.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:19.210
Oh, so that's what the sweet
bean jam was all about.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:21.620
Good luck.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.330
Thank you for your help.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:29.420
I wonder who she'll give it to...

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:30.850
Oh!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.810
Quit loitering and get home already!

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:42.360
R-Really? That old man is Amami's...

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.370
I never would've guessed she's into older men...

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.870
This has to be a mistake!

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:52.120
I know! He must not be human!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.620
Y-Yamada?

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:55.630
Chill out, you idiot!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.630
Um, everyone?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.390
If you're really serious, we won't object.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:09.890
What?

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.140
Th-That's right. Age is just a number!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.460
Good luck, Amami!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.150
U-Um...

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.900
No! He's not human, is h—

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.530
Give it a rest!

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.330
Well, today's the big day.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.330
Yeah!

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.090
This is the greatest day of the year to be a man!

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.890
These are obviously obligatory!

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.840
His appetite is his first priority.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.580
Why...

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:32.450
Why does the great Yoshida
not have a single chocolate?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.800
Of course, the ladies are too shy!

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:41.150
They can't work up the nerve to give
me chocolate on Valentine's Day.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.290
There's no need to be shy.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:47.820
Yoshida welcomes your advances
any time you're ready!

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.100
Did you just feel a chill?

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.080
Yeah.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:57.080
Forget that. What about Amami?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.590
Oh, yeah!

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.130
She's really giving them to someone.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.760
There's no telling what'll happen.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.300
He might yell at Amami.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.340
The grumpy old man, of all people...

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.110
They've still got it all wrong.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:33.870
Hibby just went to see the old lady.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.120
Then who is the gift for?

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.650
Wh-What the hell? Are you stalking me?

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:41.190
That's so creepy!

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.630
I-I am merely concerned about
Lady Amami's well-being.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.500
If something were to happen to her...

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:53.170
I'm certainly not curious about the
target of Lady Amami's affections.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:57.390
Still, one cannot help but wonder who it might be...

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.440
Creeper.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.060
Huh?

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.410
What is it?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.470
This leads to...

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.870
Is she going to the park?

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:14.520
Is that a problem?

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:17.630
Well, shouldn't she be done with the park now?

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:20.570
She only went to ask about
the chocolate recipe before.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:24.610
Then it means her special one awaits at the park.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.170
So they're meeting in the park?!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:27.180
We gotta go see!
So they're meeting in the park?!

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:30.670
We gotta go see!

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.610
Amami's finally gonna confess her love...

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:44.050
What's going on?

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.190
The old man's not there...

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.720
Amami!

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.770
Over there!

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.860
Excuse me! Please, stop him!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.310
Stop this passer-by?

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:55.170
Okay.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:57.970
What the—

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.130
Just the wind?

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.650
Sir!

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.820
Please take these.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.740
What?!

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.120
What?!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.880
Why's she giving them to that old guy?

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.870
Lady Uehara and the others
guessed correctly, after all.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.660
Good lord...

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:32.380
What is this about?
What are you giving to me?

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:37.630
Th-These are...

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.640
I made them with your wife's recipe.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:42.980
What?

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.210
You...

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.140
I'm sorry if I'm meddling.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:49.410
But...

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.490
She wanted...

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.040
to give them to you again this year.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.380
My wife passed away a year ago...

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:13.840
You're quite the strange girl.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.930
Well, I'm not one to waste food. I'll take them.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.810
Thank you very much.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.560
Terrible! Absolutely terrible!

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.960
So that was it.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:48.330
Lady Amami, you're so kind-hearted!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.990
We finally caught you!

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:55.090
So, how'd it go?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:58.090
I won't accept this! I won't!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:19:59.680
Amami?

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:03.890
Amami...

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.970
Ch-Cheer up!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.230
I'm positive your feelings got through to him!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:14.200
Y-Yeah, don't look so down.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.130
So this was another ghost thing, after all?

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.490
I guess so.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:20.990
Your father

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.490
will never accept this!

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.780
When did you become her father?

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:30.930
I wanna eat Amami's chocolate, too!

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:31.760
I want it! I want it! I want it!

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:32.510
A tantrum now?!

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.760
Are you a man or a child?!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.760
Here.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.350
Amami...

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:48.520
I made enough for everyone.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.520
Including you two.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.270
All right! A Valentine's party
with chocolates made by Amami!

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.030
Yeah!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.530
Good for you, Inoue.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:05.530
Wh-Why only me again?

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.770
Jeez!

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:05.130
They were delicious, dear...

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:44.410
Good grief. I'm bound to this preview now, too?

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:46.520
Such is the fate of a bound spirit, I suppose.

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:50.600
It's already been a year since we met?

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:53.530
I've long since been free from the concept of time,

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:55.490
but it hasn't been a bad year.

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:58.530
So, she's moved up to the next grade.

00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:01.120
I wonder how that will work out.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:04.880
Next time on Re-Kan!:
"We've Entered Our Second Year."

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:06.630
Come and watch...

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:09.240
Sorry, force of habit.
